87531e49 (1783 1793492250397 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f356") (src . "test: fixture signal sends verified before they go\n\nA census of the fixtures' signal sends (185 over test/*.sc, *.pl and\nrun-fixtures.sh) found two that verify the pid before sending, 56 that\nsend to a pid read earlier with no check at that moment, seven pkill\npatterns that end right after the run's pid digits, and one pkill with\nnothing of the run in it. A pid is reused once its process is gone, so a\nsend to a pid read for a child that has since exited can reach an\nunrelated process, and a pattern without a delimiter after the pid also\nstops the daemons of a run whose pid begins with the same digits. This\nis the first slice: the sends that normally reach an exited pid and the\none beside them on the same pid file, the eight patterns, and an audit\nthat holds them.\n\ntest/signal-send.ss, new, is daemon-idle's registry moved out: started!\nrecords a pid with its start instant (ps -o lstart=), and signal! sends\nonly when the pid is registered, answers kill -0 and still has that\ninstant; otherwise it prints \"NOTE <sig> to <pid> not sent: already\ngone\" and sends nothing. It depends on nothing the including file\ndefines; daemon-idle and daemon-namespace include it in place of their\ncopies, their rows and lines unchanged. A pid is registered while its\nprocess is expected alive: right after the spawn, or, for a pid file a\nprocess inside an inner run writes itself, by awaiting the file before\nwaiting for the run to finish; a registration made once the process may\nbe gone would record whatever holds the pid then, and the check would\npass for it. launch-self's descendant, expected gone before its file can\nbe read, registers no instant then and is not sent.\n\nThe sends moved onto signal!: log15 (the barrier children, four sends),\nlaunch-self and runner-self stop-pid!, cli2's holder that never parked,\nf0-ondemand's daemon at the end. retire-race's EXIT traps are generated\nshell text and make the same check inline: each child's lstart is\ncaptured right after it starts and kill9_if_same sends only when the pid\nanswers kill -0 and still has it. The seven patterns end where the real\ncommand line does (serve <here>/, dmn-run[0-9]*-<pid>[.]sc,\ndmn-store-<pid>( |$)), and the pgrep that asserts on the same pattern\n(daemon-e1's count, mcp-shell's survivors) takes the tightened one,\nbound once; liveness-streams' second pkill names this run's stores,\nwhere it matched any subscriber whose command line carried that text, of\nany run or any user.\n\nTests: test/signal-audit.sc, new, 19 rows: SA-0 counts the files it\nscanned and refuses fewer than the census's 255; SA-1 no pkill pattern\nends right after a name that ends in the run's pid; SA-2 no pkill\npattern is a literal with nothing of the run in it; SA-3, per converted\nfile, the bare sends left are exactly a declared remainder, each named\nwith its census row and slice, and the checked form is present; SA-4\nruns signal! itself: an ended process (held on a go-file until\nregistered) is not signalled, a running one is and ends, an unregistered\none is not, and one whose recorded instant differs is not until the true\none is restored. Red first on the base with the new files alone: 14 of\n19 rows (SA-1, with the seven hits; SA-2, with its one; both SA-3 rows\nof each of the six files). A \"loud\" base with the sends' 2>/dev/null\ndropped prints \"No such process\" one for one with the NOTEs the new tree\nprints (log15 2, launch-self 3, runner-self 7). A mutant without the\ninstant comparison reds SA-4's identity row and daemon-idle's CONTROL\nrow. The touched fixtures keep their rows; their line counts grow by the\nNOTEs. A live check of each tightened pattern: the real forms match, a\nrun whose pid has this one's as a prefix does not. Reviewed in two\nrounds; the second registers runner-self's inner pids before the run\nfinishes and holds SA-4's ended child until it is registered.\ntest/RUN.md's list of the non-.sc files a delivery carries gains\nsignal-send.ss; rows-baseline.txt takes new hashes for the 15 touched\nfixtures and a line for signal-audit.\n\nStage on an isolated copy of the tree (240 fixtures): only the known\npair red (f0-ondemand COST-1 over its budget, startup-ratio C1/C3);\nthree python fixtures run; row baseline hashes all the described\nversions, line counts as predicted except liveness, untouched, one line\nfewer; no process of the run left; alternation of the compiled product\nagainst the base median 0.9985 (p10 ratios 0.9980, 0.9985, 1.0146),\nwithin 1%.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 574))))
